? WIP;
? Made by the head dev of Awsta's Dev Emporium/ head dev of AWScript
(this language btw!)

This PureInt module implements math purely in AWScript, which doesn't come with math defaults.
This should probably not be used for big projects if _ functions are exposed by your dialect of AWScript. 

This uses periods to help organize in the names of @Lockers, these serve ZERO syntactic purpose.

Requires Awsta.Logic, import prior to this;

new @Locker Awsta.PureInt;
mount Awsta.PureInt;

announce #DiagnosticMode;
set #DiagnosticMode to false;

announce #Input.Number1;
set #Input.Number1 to 0;

announce #Input.Number2;
set #Input.Number2 to 0;

announce #Input.Operand;
set #Input.Operand to 0;

announce #Output.Number;
set #Output.Number to 0;

announce #Input.Resolution;
set #Input.Resolution to 6;

? Input format is x operand y, without spaces so like 40+10, Resolution is the amount of bits;

? SAdd2 (simple adder 2) function uses HARDCODED 6-bit integers, as we must start with hardcoding.
Why? Well we cannot iterate through a loop before we can add or substract

mount Awsta.PureInt;
new @Function CleanupTemp;
construct CleanupTemp;
> disavow @Locker Awsta.PureInt.Temp;

new @Function SAdd2;
construct SAdd2;
> mount Awsta.PureInt;
> new @Locker Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #FirstBin in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #SecondBin in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #A0 in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #A1 in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #B0 in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #B1 in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #TotalBinarySum in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #Carry0 in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> announce #Temp in Awsta.PureInt.Temp;

> basetwo #Input.Number1 to #FirstBin@Awsta.PureInt.Temp resolution 2;
> basetwo #Input.Number2 to #SecondBin@Awsta.PureInt.Temp resolution 2;

> slice #FirstBin@Awsta.PureInt.Temp at 2 to #A0@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> slice #FirstBin@Awsta.PureInt.Temp at 1 to #A1@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> slice #SecondBin@Awsta.PureInt.Temp at 2 to #B0@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> slice #SecondBin@Awsta.PureInt.Temp at 1 to #B1@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;

? Bit 0;

> set #Input.A in Awsta.Logic to #A0@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> set #Input.B in Awsta.Logic to #B0@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> run XOR in Awsta.Logic;
> perchance #Output.Result@Awsta.Logic is 1;
> / set #TotalBinarySum in Awsta.PureInt.Temp to 1;
> \ set #TotalBinarySum in Awsta.PureInt.Temp to 0;

> set #Input.A in Awsta.Logic to #A0@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> set #Input.B in Awsta.Logic to #B0@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> run AND in Awsta.Logic;
> perchance #Output.Result@Awsta.Logic is 1;
> / set #Carry0 in Awsta.PureInt.Temp to 1;
> \ set #Carry0 in Awsta.PureInt.Temp to 0;

? Bit 1;

> set #Input.A in Awsta.Logic to #A1@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> set #Input.B in Awsta.Logic to #B1@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> run XOR in Awsta.Logic;

> perchance #Output.Result@Awsta.Logic is 1;
> / set #Temp in Awsta.PureInt.Temp to 1;
> \ set #Temp in Awsta.PureInt.Temp to 0;

> set #Input.A in Awsta.Logic to #Temp@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> set #Input.B in Awsta.Logic to #Carry0@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> run XOR in Awsta.Logic;

> perchance #Output.Result@Awsta.Logic is 1;
> / concat 1 with #TotalBinarySum@Awsta.PureInt.Temp to #TotalBinarySum@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;
> \ concat 0 with #TotalBinarySum@Awsta.PureInt.Temp to #TotalBinarySum@Awsta.PureInt.Temp;

> baseten #TotalBinarySum@Awsta.PureInt.Temp to #Output.Number;

> run CleanupTemp;
> dismount;

dismount;
